# =============================================================================
# bypass_paligemma_auth.patch
# =============================================================================
# Purpose:
#   Bypass HF gate on google/paligemma-3b-pt-224 so BridgeVLA's MVT can
#   construct its PaliGemma backbone without authenticated download.
#
# Strategy:
#   - Use the ungated fal/paligemma-3b-mix-224 repo (same Gemma tokenizer +
#     PaliGemma-3B architecture). Download is ~10MB for config+tokenizer.
#   - Construct PaliGemmaForConditionalGeneration from config only (random
#     init in bf16). RLBench fine-tune ckpt model_80.pth contains all 604
#     PaliGemma weight tensors and overwrites these random weights via
#     load_state_dict() at agent setup.
#   - In `load_pretrain=True` branch, gracefully skip BridgeVLA pretrain-
#     stage safetensors load when its path isn't on disk (we don't have
#     those weights, but it's fine — RLBench fine-tune ckpt is complete).
#
# Verified at design time (in container):
#   PaliGemmaForConditionalGeneration(AutoConfig.from_pretrained(
#     "fal/paligemma-3b-mix-224"
#   )).load_state_dict({k[len("mvt1.model."):]: v for k,v in
#                       model_80.pth['model_state'].items()
#                       if k.startswith("mvt1.model.")}, strict=False)
#   returns 0 missing / 0 unexpected.
#
# Apply (idempotent via --forward):
#   cd /workspace/BridgeVLA/finetune
#   patch -p1 --forward < bypass_paligemma_auth.patch
# =============================================================================
